# Jak II: the menu pointer on the title's menu (LIST-0.1.1 item 19; the owner: "i want the pointer to be able to
# interact with all menus"), with Jak II's multiplayer on, as it starts: the title's five rows (New Game, Load Game,
# Multiplayer, Options, Quit Game; jak2_ptr_menu_mpoff.sim is the four with it off). Start, then A once the title is
# ready (as jak2_melee.sim), opens its menu; the right hand turns from high to low (the dot down the panel 1.6 m
# ahead), a shot each 5 degrees: the row under the dot is the one picked (highlighted). Then the dot back on the lowest
# row (Quit Game; at -20 it is under the menu, where the trigger picks nothing) and the trigger: its Yes / No line comes
# up under it. Then at 0, -2 and -4 degrees (the line is a little under the row's name, its middle 333.5 with five rows,
# 301.5 with four: JAKVR_POINTER_TRACE=1 logs the dot against it; the dot is on it within 18 of its middle, and at 2
# degrees, over Quit Game's name, a click on the row's right third is a step) the dot to the left half (12 degrees:
# Yes) and the right half (-4: No; -12 is past the line's end), a shot each, and last the trigger on No at -2, which
# closes the question (a click on Yes would quit the game). b64: the title's version line, the mod's own, reads
# "JaD2MP (v0.3.1-jakvr.0.1.3)" (who joins whom).
2400 menu 1
2406 menu 0
